# Track Training Journal Privacy Policy

**Last updated: October 1, 2026**

Track Training Journal is a personal project developed by Lucas to record running and track-and-field workouts and explore relationships between training, recovery, and physiological measurements.

## Information Collected

When the account owner connects their WHOOP account and authorizes access, the project may retrieve sleep measurements, recovery scores, heart rate variability, resting heart rate, physiological-cycle data, strain, and workout summaries.

The project may also store manually entered information, including workout distances, repetition times, rest intervals, lifting sessions, perceived effort, soreness, training habits, and notes.

The project stores authorization tokens needed to access WHOOP data. It does not collect or store the account owner’s WHOOP password.

## How Information Is Used

Information is used to display a personal training dashboard, maintain a workout journal, calculate trends, and investigate relationships between training habits, physiological measurements, and performance.

Analysis is intended to support personal training decisions. It does not provide medical diagnoses or establish that an observed correlation is causal.

